---
layout: base.njk
title: Fees
description: Plain pricing, no packages you don't need. Final figures from Sarah.
---

{#- TODO-SARAH: the prices. All three are the design's placeholder — a euro sign
    and an em dash, no figure.

    A list plus a loop rather than three copy-pasted cards, the same call
    testimonials.njk and header.njk make: the markup is identical every time and
    only the strings differ.

    featured is the one flag that decides which card gets the purple outline and
    the "Most booked" badge.  -#}
{% set services = [
  {
    "name": "Career coaching session",
    "price": "€—",
    "detail": "60 minutes, one-to-one. Goal setting and next steps.",
    "featured": true
  },
  {
    "name": "CV & cover letter review",
    "price": "€—",
    "detail": "Written feedback plus a rewritten draft."
  },
  {
    "name": "Mock interview",
    "price": "€—",
    "detail": "Realistic practice with structured feedback."
  }
] %}
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-head__title">Fees</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lead">Plain pricing, no packages you don't need. Final figures from Sarah.</p>
</div>
<ul class="fees">
  {%- for s in services %}
    {#- The badge is real text and comes first, as the design draws it, so the card
      reads "Most booked, Career coaching session". 
 -#}
    <li class="card{% if s.featured %} card--featured{% endif %}">
      {%- if s.featured %}<span class="fee__badge">Most booked</span>{%- endif %}
      <div class="fee__row">
        <h2 class="card__title">{{ s.name }}</h2>
        <p class="fee__price">{{ s.price }}</p>
      </div>
      <p class="card__note">{{ s.detail }}</p>
    </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
<div class="fee-cta">
  <a class="button" href="/book/">Book a consultation</a>
  <p class="fee-cta__note">Not sure which fits? Start with the free intro call.</p>
</div>
